-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  dir_addsourcefile_header.pcpp - pcpp: a header warning seen by two translation units

  A cli test: pcpp runs itself with the args (in the suite's output root,
  -o "$P:output" so the build lands there), on the fixture named; its
  output and exit code are the check. Both translation units include fixtures\\dir_cli_shared_warn.h: its
  warning is one report (at the header line), not one per unit, with
  the include step of the first unit in build order (the .cpp).
*******************************************************************************/

module exe dir_addsourcefile_header;

/*
  @@test
    kind cli
    args "--no-banner <DIR>/fixtures/dir_cli_shared_warn.pcpp -o $P:output"
    exitcode 0
    expect
    | Compiling <DIR>/fixtures/dir_cli_shared_warn.pcpp
    | Target platform: x86_64-windows-gnu
    | Optimize level: debug
    | Subsystem: Console
    | Saving build file...
    | Building dir_cli_shared_warn...
    | [WARN] <DIR>/fixtures/dir_cli_shared_warn.h(23,2) ZB0016: dir_cli_shared: one header warning
    |   <DIR>/fixtures/dir_cli_shared_warn.cpp(22,10): Note: in file included from <DIR>/fixtures/dir_cli_shared_warn.cpp:22:
    | Build succeeded.
    | Output: <OUT>/bin/dir_cli_shared_warn.exe
  @@end
*/

begin
end.
